    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0203" n="191" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg191"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to
                        Lieutenant General Albert C.
                    Wedemeyer</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-01-17">17 January 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>67. Thanks for your complete statement of demobilization views in 20304. I still
                    would like a concise statement from you to be quoted by me to Generalissimo
                    regarding confusion of understanding which has arisen over your statement to
                    Sixth Army Commander requested in first half of last sentence my 52.<anchor
                        n="61" xml:id="d68-f1"/> I do not think it wise to use your 20060 because of
                    reference to armies in third sentence.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
